# StoryTool — Figma ↔ Code sync

## Quick commands

| What | Command |
|---|---|
| Pull Figma Variables → `design-tokens.css` | `npm run figma:pull` |
| Push `design-tokens.css` → Figma Variables | `npm run figma:push` |
| Regenerate `design-tokens.json` from CSS | `npm run sync-tokens` |

## Figma → CSS pull (`figma:pull`)

- Script: `scripts/figma-to-tokens.mjs`
- Requires `FIGMA_TOKEN` in `.env.local` (see `.env.local.example`)
- Reads Figma Variables via REST API (`GET /v1/files/:fileKey/variables/local`)
- Maps variable names back to CSS custom properties using `CSS_VAR_MAP` in the script
- Rewrites the `:root {}` block in `design-tokens.css` in-place (preserves comments)
- Automatically re-runs `sync-tokens` to keep `design-tokens.json` in sync
- **After pulling:** reload the browser; no build step needed

## CSS → Figma push (`figma:push`)

- Script: `scripts/build-figma-variables-snippet.mjs`
- Generates `scripts/figma-variables-use-figma.generated.js`
- That file must be executed via Figma MCP (`use_figma` tool) — read `figma-use` skill first
- Creates / updates collections: **StoryTool/Color**, **Layout**, **Motion**, **Typography**

## Code Connect mappings

- File: `figma/code-connect.json`
- Maps every Figma component to its HTML selector, source file, design tokens, and child anatomy
- **Components covered:**
  - `SpineBar` → `#spine` in `index.html`
  - `LeftPanel` → `#left-panel` in `index.html`
  - `NodeLibItem` → `renderLib()` in `script.js`
  - `NodeCard` → `createNode()` in `script.js` (5 variants: world, character, director, scene, narrative)
  - `RightPanel` → `#right-panel` in `index.html` (CONFIG / SCRIPT / ROOM tabs)
  - `PromptDock` → `#prompt-dock` in `index.html` (collapsed + expanded states)
  - `ProgressBar` → `#progress-bar` in `index.html`
  - `FTUXIntroOverlay` → `#ftux-intro` in `index.html`
  - `FTUXTipBox` → `#ftux-tip-box` in `index.html`
  - `CanvasGrid` → `draw()` in `script.js`
  - `Icon` → `ICONS` object in `script.js`
  - `SpotifyBar` → `#dock-spotify-bar` in `index.html`

## Icon system

- All icons are inline SVGs from the `ICONS` object in `script.js` (Material Design Icons)
- Always `fill="currentColor"` — color is inherited from parent via `currentColor`
- Wrapper: `<span class="ic">` — `display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; flex-shrink:0`
- **No background frame** — icons are bare SVGs, never wrapped in a colored circle/square
- Size contexts: spine-btn=14px, node-head-icon=14px, lib-icon=14px, dock buttons=11–12px
- Figma: use instances of `icon/{name}` components from the **Icons** page

## Token rules

- **Never** hardcode a hex or rgba value in new CSS — add a token to `design-tokens.css` first
- Category colors: `--c-world` `--c-char` `--c-director` `--c-scene` `--c-narrative` `--c-default`
- Motion: all durations and easings are tokens (`--dur-*`, `--ease-*`)
- Layout: `--grid-size`, `--panel-w`, `--spine-h`, `--progress-bar-h`, `--dock-gap`, `--dock-shell-h-inset`

